  "question": {
    "text": "An object <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> is kept in front of two plane mirrors as shown in the figure. The number of images formed is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math>. Find out the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math>.\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/70p.PNG\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 166px;\" /></p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/llxuiihljmadrfgssxcolhnkcqncxqcansgvlqnmgqrfvintke.png\" /></p><p>The above diagram represents the angular positions of possible images that can be formed in the given case. Since, images further than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn><mo>°</mo></math>&nbsp;will not be visible, we obtain the maximum number&nbsp;of visible images as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>.</p>",
